# GUI parity (same-PR rule)

## Hosts (all four)

| Host | Path |
| --- | --- |
| egui | `crates/app` |
| SpecChumMac | `apps/macos` + `living_room` / `host_api` |
| Windows shell | `crates/windows_shell` ([#351](https://github.com/mward-sudo/spec_chum/issues/351)) |
| Linux shell | `crates/linux_shell` ([#351](https://github.com/mward-sudo/spec_chum/issues/351)) |

## Must

- Same **product** features on every first-party GUI host unless genuinely platform-specific
- Shared behaviour in `control_plane` / `host_api` / `machine`; hosts are thin adapters
- GUI/agent-visible change → update **every** host (or shared backend) in the **same PR** + docs as needed
- **Never** silent follow-up (“egui now, Mac/Windows/Linux later”) except documented vertical-slice deferrals in #351 / `docs/WINDOWS_NATIVE.md` / `docs/LINUX_NATIVE.md`

## May differ (HIG / presentation only)

| OK to differ | Must not differ |
| --- | --- |
| Window chrome, menus, materials, spacing | Which product features exist |
| Shortcut modifiers (⌘ vs Ctrl) for same action | Action meaning / guest behaviour |
| File-dialog look | Filters / formats / load semantics |
| Blit path (egui / Metal / GDI / GTK) | Framebuffer contents / timing ownership |

## Finish check

- Grep: `crates/app`, `apps/macos`, `crates/windows_shell`, `crates/linux_shell`, living_room agent FFI
- `SPEC_CHUM_AGENT=1`: verify all host embed paths
- Rebuild touched hosts (`build_macos_app.sh` / Windows / Linux scripts as applicable)
- Missing feature on any host (outside explicit slice deferral) → work not finished
